{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":1262697,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,7]],"date-time":"2026-10-07T18:55:18Z","timestamp":1791399318276,"version":"4.3.3"},"reference-count":29,"publisher":"Institute of Mathematical Statistics","issue":"3","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Ann. Probab."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,5,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>For an inverse temperature \u03b2&gt;0, we define the \u03b2-circular Riesz gas on Rd as any microscopic thermodynamic limit of Gibbs particle systems on the torus interacting via the Riesz potential g(x)=\u2016x\u2016\u2212s. We focus on the nonintegrable case d\u22121&lt;s&lt;d. Our main result ensures, for any dimension d\u22651 and inverse temperature \u03b2&gt;0, the existence of a \u03b2-circular Riesz gas which is not number-rigid. Recall that a point process is said number rigid if the number of points in a bounded Borel set \u0394 is a function of the point configuration outside \u0394. It is the first time that the nonnumber-rigidity is proved for a Gibbs point process interacting via a nonintegrable potential. We follow a statistical physics approach based on the canonical DLR equations. It is inspired by the recent paper (Comm. Pure Appl. Math. 74 (2021) 172\u2013222) where the authors prove the number-rigidity of the Sine\u03b2 process.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1214\/22-aop1606","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,5,2]],"date-time":"2023-05-02T03:04:57Z","timestamp":1682996697000},"page":"1025-1065","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":8,"title":["Number-rigidity and \u03b2-circular Riesz gas"],"prefix":"10.1214","volume":"51","author":[{"given":"David","family":"Dereudre","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Laboratoire Paul Painlev\u00e9, Universit\u00e9 de Lille"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Thibaut",