nding to a random parameter  we obtain quenched memory loss, decay of correlations, CLTs with rates, moment bounds, and almost sure invariance principles (ASIPs) when the essential infimum of  is sufficiently small and the driving process (i.e., random environment) is mixing sufficiently fast. Su obtained ASIP for ergodic driving systems when the essential supremum of  is less than . As will be elaborated in Section\u00a01, restrictions on the essential infimum are more natural in our context. Our results have an abstract form which we believe could be useful in other circumstances, as will be elaborated in a future work.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1112\/jlms.70707","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,16]],"date-time":"2026-09-16T18:46:34Z","timestamp":1789584394000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Decay of correlations and limit theorems for random intermittent maps"],"prefix":"10.1112","volume":"114","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-1979-4344","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Davor","family":"Dragi\u010devi\u0107","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Faculty of Mathematics University of Rijeka Rijeka Croatia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Yeor","family":"Hafouta","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Mathematics Ben\u2010Gurion University of the Negev Be'er Sheva Israel"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Juho","family":"Lepp\u00e4nen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Mathematics Tokai University Hiratsuka Kanagawa Japan"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,16]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_9_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s00440-014-0571-y"},{"key":"e_1_2_9_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.jde.2021.12.008"}